From: icanc0 <ai7@vincentxie.net>
Date: 2026-08-21
Subject: [PATCH 1/N] pcb_plotter: skip wxSafeYield in the per-layer loop for CLI

`PCB_PLOTTER::Plot` calls `wxSafeYield()` after each layer to let the GUI
event loop repaint the progress reporter. In CLI headless mode there is no
event loop, no dialog, no repaint target — the yield is pure overhead that
still enters wx's yield machinery (locks, event dispatch prep) and returns.

For a plot job over N layers this is N wasted yield cycles.

Gate on Pgm().IsGUI(). This mirrors the same signal `getBoard()` in
pcbnew_jobs_handler.cpp already uses to distinguish CLI from GUI.

Safe because:

- GUI callers still get the yield (behavior preserved for interactive plot).
- CLI has no progress dialog to repaint, and the reporter it does have
  writes directly to stdout/stderr without needing the event loop.

---
 pcbnew/pcb_plotter.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pcbnew/pcb_plotter.cpp b/pcbnew/pcb_plotter.cpp
--- a/pcbnew/pcb_plotter.cpp
+++ b/pcbnew/pcb_plotter.cpp
@@ -308,7 +308,8 @@ bool PCB_PLOTTER::Plot( const wxString& aOutputPath, const LSEQ& aLayersToPlot,
         }

         pageNum++;

-        wxSafeYield(); // displays report message.
+        if( Pgm().IsGUI() )
+            wxSafeYield(); // displays report message.
     }

     if( jobfile_writer && m_plotOpts.GetCreateGerberJobFile() )
